Brainstorming & Idea Prioritization
1. Project Background

The project focuses on implementing a secure and controlled record access system in ServiceNow using Script-Controlled Access Control Lists (ACLs).

The system is designed to restrict access to institution records based on user roles and the value of the Branch field.

2. Problem Identification

During the brainstorming process, the following problems were identified:

Unauthorized users may access institution records.
Users may need access to only specific branch-related records.
Different users require different levels of permissions.
Users should not be allowed to perform operations beyond their assigned responsibilities.
Administrators require complete access to manage the records and security configuration.
3. Ideas Considered

The following approaches were considered:

Role-Based Access Control

Access can be provided according to the roles assigned to users.

Branch-Based Access Control

Access can be restricted according to the Branch field of a record.

Script-Controlled ACL

ServiceNow scripts can be used to implement customized access-control conditions.

Separate CRUD ACLs

Different ACLs can be created for:

READ
CREATE
WRITE
DELETE
4. Selected Idea

The selected project idea is:

Script-Controlled ACL – Restrict Record Access Based on Field Value

The solution combines user roles and record field values to control access to institution records.

5. Reason for Selecting the Idea

The idea was selected because it:

Provides controlled access to records.
Helps protect institutional information.
Supports different permissions for different users.
Allows field-based record restrictions.
Supports separate READ, CREATE, WRITE, and DELETE permissions.
Allows administrators to retain full access.
6. Expected Benefits
Improved record security.
Reduced unauthorized access.
Controlled user permissions.
Better management of institutional records.
Flexible access-control configuration.
Possibility of extending the solution to other tables and requirements.
7. Project Objective

The main objective is to develop a ServiceNow ACL solution that ensures users can access and manage records only according to their assigned permissions and the defined branch-based access requirements.
